{"answers":[{"question_id":"Q003_actin_like_atpase_divergence","answer":"In SCOPe 2.08, these catalytic domains are not put in one narrow family; they are three separate families inside the same superfamily. SCOPe places Actin/HSP70 at family c.55.1.1, Hexokinase at c.55.1.3, and Glycerol kinase at c.55.1.4, all under the Actin-like ATPase domain superfamily c.55.1. That superfamily is within the Ribonuclease H-like motif fold c.55 of the alpha and beta proteins, a/b, class c.

The evolutionary inference SCOPe permits is therefore remote homology of the catalytic domains: despite very different cellular roles and substrate choices, their ATPase/kinase catalytic cores are treated as having a probable common origin within the actin-like ATPase superfamily. The correct transferable signal is the domain-level structural and mechanistic theme, especially the actin-like ATPase core, not whole-protein function.

Important limits follow from the SCOPe level. Being in c.55.1 does not make Actin/HSP70, hexokinase, and glycerol kinase the same family, so one should not directly transfer actin polymerization, HSP70 chaperone behavior, hexose phosphorylation, glycerol phosphorylation, oligomeric state, full multidomain architecture, or detailed substrate specificity across them. Likewise, the broader c.55 fold contains several superfamilies, so fold membership alone is structural resemblance and is weaker than the c.55.1 superfamily homology assignment. A template or representative from one of these families can support modeling of the conserved catalytic-domain core of another, but only as a remote template whose alignment, local insertions, active-site geometry, and family-specific features need independent checking.","evidence_used":["mcp__scope.get_scop_node /api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.55","mcp__scope.get_scop_node /api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.55/parents","mcp__scope.list_scop_children /api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.55/children?limit=20","mcp__scope.get_scop_node /api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.55.1","mcp__scope.get_scop_node /api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.55.1/parents","mcp__scope.list_scop_children /api/v1/releases/2.08/sccs/c.55.1/children?limit=20"]}]}
